=== KEY DECISIONS (documented INTERPRETATIONS) ===
1. Adjacency default = eight (8-neighbourhood within a hall) to match the legacy
   formulation and make Phase D equivalence meaningful; cardinal supported.
2. Soft objective = minimize adjacent OCCUPIED same-department seat pairs (§11-compatible);
   forced to 0 under DEPARTMENT_ONLY / STRICT_DEPT_OR_YEAR, meaningful under COHORT.
3. All domain candidates are seated (sum_s X[c,s] == 1); capacity guaranteed by the
   composition guard before CP-SAT (candidateCount > seatCount => ERR_INSUFFICIENT_DOMAIN_CAPACITY).
4. Error-code extension (documented in spec §39.2.8): ERR_INVALID_POLICY_CONFIGURATION
   for policies requiring a 'year' attribute when candidates lack one.
5. Composition year/cohort risk flagged only when >=2 distinct buckets exist (a single
   year is structure, not imbalance).
6. Candidate-to-domain allocation is a deterministic balanced helper (benchmark/scheduling
   shape); the orchestrator owns allocation at deployment (§11.1). Allocation never splits
   a connected component and never uses department as a hard partitioning rule.

